(a) whether Government has granted a two-year exemption to certain China-linked power equipment manufacturers to participate in tenders for critical power projects and, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the reasons for granting such exemption and the benefits expected in terms of timely completion of power projects, reduction in costs, technology transfer and strengthening of domestic manufacturing; and 
(c) whether Government has assessed the impact of such exemption on Indian power equipment manufacturers, and if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether the Central Government is aware of the strong objections raised by Government of Tamil Nadu to the latest guidelines issued by Government Central Water Commission for appraisal of water resources projects in the Cauvery Basin, including the presumptive concurrence clause;
(b) whether these guidelines were issued without consultation with Tamil Nadu and other lower riparian States, if so, the reasons therefor; and
(c) whether Government has taken note of Tamil Nadu’s urgent demand for constitution of a Tribunal based on representation dated 4th March, 2026 on the proposed Mekedatu project for adjudication of dispute, as the Mekadatu project contrary to judgement?

(a) the details of financial assistance provided by the Central Government for promotion and development of football during the last five years, scheme-wise, State wise and year-wise;
(b) the details of football infrastructure, academies, High Performance Centres and grassroots development programmes supported by Government, State-wise; and
(c) whether Government has prepared a long-term roadmap to improve India's FIFA ranking and qualify for the FIFA World Cup through enhanced infrastructure, international collaborations and talent development programmes and if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has received representations from Government of Tamil Nadu seeking approval for new National Highway projects, road widening, bypasses, flyovers and other road infrastructure works;
(b) if so, the details of the projects proposed and pending projects, district-wise, together with the estimated cost and present status of each proposal;
(c) the number of proposals approved, pending and rejected, along with the reasons therefor;
(d) the timeline fixed for according approvals and completing the sanctioned projects; and
(e) the total funds allocated to Tamil Nadu for National Highway development during the last five years, year-wise and project-wise?

(a) whether any grain storage godowns have been sanctioned, inaugurated or approved under the World's Largest Grain Storage Plan (WLGSP) in Tamil Nadu and, if so, the details thereof, district-wise;
(b) the total funds allocated, released and utilised under the scheme, State-wise;
(c) the total storage capacity proposed and created, indicating the number of Primary Agricultural Credit Societies (PACS) covered, State-wise;
(d) the timeline fixed for completion of the sanctioned projects; and
(e) the number of direct and indirect employment opportunities expected to be generated through the initiatives launched by the Ministry during its five years of establishment, along with the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has reduced the Rice allocation under the Antyodaya Anna Yojana (AAY) and if so, the details thereof, State-wise;
(b) the quantity of Rice allocated and lifted by Tamil Nadu under AAY during the last three years, year-wise, along with the reasons for any shortfall; and
(c) whether Government proposes to revise the Rice allocation under AAY and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of ethanol manufacturing units established in the country, State-wise, along with their production capacity;
(b) the details of incentives, subsidies and tax exemptions provided by Government for ethanol production during the last five years;
(c) whether Government has assessed the impact of E20 petrol on fuel efficiency, vehicle performance and consumer expenditure and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the steps taken to address the challenges in implementing the Ethanol Blended Petrol (EBP) Programme?

(a) whether Government has received any proposal from the Tamil Nadu Housing Board (TNHB) under Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana–Urban (PMAY-U) 2.0 during 2026 and if so, the details thereof;
(b) the number of houses sanctioned, completed and occupied under PMAY-U in the State of Tamil Nadu, along with the funds allocated, released and utilised, year-wise;
(c) the reasons for the delay, if any, in sanctioning proposals or releasing funds under PMAY-U 2.0; and
(d) whether Government proposes to expedite approvals and enhance financial assistance under PMAY-U 2.0 in view of the rising cost of land and construction in urban areas and if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has received a proposal from Government of Tamil Nadu for the revamp, transfer and integration of the Chennai Mass Rapid Transit System (MRTS) with Chennai Metro Rail Limited and if so, the details and status thereof;
(b) the funds sought by Government of Tamil Nadu and the funds sanctioned, allocated and released by the Central Government for the MRTS revamp and integration project, State and year-wise; and
(c) whether the Ministry has coordinated with Chennai Metro Rail Limited to improve multimodal connectivity, including the proposed commercial development at Thirumangalam Metro Station, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has directed electric vehicle manufacturers to strengthen cybersecurity audits of battery management systems, if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether Government proposes to introduce mandatory battery safety testing and certification standards, including crash impact, thermal runaway, water immersion and fast-charging tests, similar to vehicle crash tests;
(c) the details of safety standards presently applicable to Electric Vehicle (EV) batteries;
(d) whether any Central funds have been allocated for battery safety testing infrastructure and research; and
(e) any timeline fixed for implementation of the proposed safety measures?
