(c) the details of recommendations made by the Supreme Court Collegium that have been pending with Government for more than one year, including the names of recommended candidates, the dates of recommendation and the reasons for delay?

(a) whether the Central Government has rejected or disputed air quality data published by certain internationally reputed organisations claiming India as 5th polluted country and the reasons therefor;
(b) the month-wise and city-wise official Air Quality Index (AQI) data for the past 36 months for the ten most polluted cities in the country, area-wise details for Delhi, along with pollutant-wise parameters; and
(c) the prescribed air quality standards as per World Health Organization guidelines and the corresponding levels recorded in these cities?

(a) the targets and actual training/placement numbers under Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY) 4.0 and other schemes for Tamil Nadu during 2024-25 and 2025-26, State-wise details thereof;
(b) whether Government is aware of CAG-noted implementation failures, unspent funds nationally and low Central releases affecting Tamil Nadu’s youth skilling ecosystem despite the State’s high startup ranking;
(c) the details of any pending Union share or unutilised funds for Tamil Nadu Skill Development Corporation; and
(d) the immediate action to clear pending dues and allocate higher targets to Tamil Nadu without regional disparity?

(a) the State-wise details of funds allocated and released under National Cooperative Development Corporation (NCDC) schemes and the National Cooperative Policy, 2025 during 2024–25 and 2025–26, including the share of Tamil Nadu vis-à-vis other major States;
(b) whether any proposal from cooperatives in Tamil Nadu is pending or delayed, if so, the reasons therefor;
(c) the criteria adopted for allocation and release of central assistance to States; and
(d) the steps taken to ensure timely release of eligible funds and equitable treatment of all States, including Tamil Nadu?

