(b) whether Government has received complaints from families for repatriation of Indians who have died overseas; and
(c) the details of such complaints, action taken thereon and the steps taken to prevent financial hardship and ensure dignified assistance to bereaved families?

(a) whether Government has examined the issue of freight movement in the country being predominantly road-led, with nearly 65 per cent of freight traffic carried by road transport, resulting in traffic congestion, modal imbalance, higher logistics costs and increased carbon intensity due to rail bottlenecks and inadequate first and last-mile connectivity;
(b) whether any assessment has been undertaken regarding its impact on emissions, logistics efficiency and supply-chain competitiveness and steps taken to address the issues; and
(c) whether Government has considered to promote multimodal integration, improve road-rail-coastal connectivity, strengthen driver training, safety and rest infrastructure, if so, the steps taken, State-wise?

(a) the State-wise and year-wise details of damage assessment reports submitted by States/UTs seeking NDRF funds and NDRF assistance released since 2021;
(b) the reasons for delay, if any, in release of NDRF funds to certain States;
(c) whether Government has prescribed timelines, procedures or Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) for damage assessment and release of NDRF assistance; and
(d) reasons for sanctioning only ?285.54 crore and ?397.13 crore against Tamil Nadu’s request of ?37,907 crore for losses due to Cyclone Michaung and subsequent floods, details of report and reason rejecting each damages sought by State of Tamil Nadu request?

(a) the details of projects approved, initiated and proposed under the Maritime Amrit Kaal Vision 2047 across the country, including port development, shipbuilding, ship repair, coastal shipping, inland waterways and allied maritime infrastructure;
(b) the names of States where new ports, shipyards and maritime clusters are proposed, along with project-wise financial outlay;
(c) if so, the details of the specific projects sanctioned or proposed for the State of Tamil Nadu, including the proposed shipbuilding cluster, new shipyard and associated infrastructure; and
(d) the details of the estimated number of direct and indirect employment opportunities likely to be generated, State-wise and project-wise?

(a) whether small businesses in India are facing increasing operational and regulatory pressures due to rising compliance requirements, limited access to finance, structural disadvantages in competing with larger enterprises, low awareness of Government support and incentive schemes, and growing expectations to meet social and environmental impact standards;
(b) whether any assessment has been undertaken to study the impact of these challenges on the sustainability and growth of small enterprises; and
(c) if so, the measures that are proposed to simplify compliance, improve access to credit, enhance awareness of schemes and strengthen institutional support for small businesses in the country?

(a) whether the Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) proposed to be signed between the Chennai Mass Rapid Transit System (MRTS) and Chennai Metro Rail Limited (CMRL) for the takeover and integration of MRTS has been finalised, if so, the status of the merger and the reasons for the delay in signing the MoU;
(b) the details of pending railways projects as on 01.02.2026 in Tamil Nadu, budget allocated, present status, the reasons for delay; and
(c) whether a fresh tender has been proposed for the Athipattu–Gummidipoondi section for additional track expansion, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the details of action taken on feasibility study for establishing regional benches of Supreme Court;
(b) the steps taken by Government to ensure social diversity and social representation in appointment of judges in higher judiciary and number of SC, ST, OBC, general, women and minority judges appointed in HCs and SC since 2021; and
(c) the category-wise composition of judges in the Supreme Court and High Courts as on 01.02.2026, and the vacancies of judges in each High Court, as on date?

(a) the details of funds approved by project approval board and released under Samagra Shiksha Scheme during last five years, State-wise and year-wise;
(b) whether despite the Parliamentary Standing Committee on EWCY&S has urged the Union Government to release pending funds for the Samagra Shiksha Abhiyan (SSA) to States like West Bengal, Kerala and Tamil Nadu, deeming it unjustified to withhold funds over disagreements on NEP, 2020 or PM SHRI schools, if so, the reasons for not releasing the fund; and
(c) the manner in which schools are being established and the funds shared by Government are in compliance with Sections 6 and 7 of RTE Act, 2009?

(a) the total number of Primary Agricultural Credit Societies (PACS) in the country, State-wise, particularly in the State of Tamil Nadu, along with the number of PACS whose statutory audits have been completed during the last five financial years, year-wise;
(b) the number of PACS where audits are pending or long-pending beyond the prescribed time-limit, State-wise and the reasons for such delay including shortage of auditors, lack of trained personnel or non-completion of computerisation; and
(c) whether it is a fact that a substantial number of PACS are still not undergoing on-system or digital audits despite being covered under the PACS Computerisation Scheme?

(a) whether Government has taken steps to reduce the overburdening of Tier-I cities caused by rapid urbanisation due to migration, non-farm employment and growth of the services sector, and to promote the development of small towns;
(b) whether any assessment has been made of the impact of such urbanisation beyond the scope of AMRUT and AMRUT 2.0;
(c) whether existing urban schemes adequately cover new small towns other than Tier-I cities, and if so, the details of infrastructure funds allocatted to such identified towns, and if not, the reasons therefor; and
(d) the steps proposed, to strengthen urban local bodies?

(a) whether the Parliamentary Standing Committee, in its March, 2025 report, flagged serious under-utilisation of funds under the National Overseas Scholarship (NOS) and SHREYAS scheme and delayed scholarship disbursal; 
(b) if so, the details of budget allotted, revised budget and actual expenditure for the last five years under these schemes and reasons therefor;
(c) whether the Committee observed that the annual scholarship amount is insufficient to meet current student expenses;
(d) if so, the details of present scholarship amount and how it has been revised during last five years and steps taken; and
(e) the details of steps taken to increase the seats under NOS scheme?

(a) whether Government has raised concerns with the Sri Lankan Government regarding Sections 14(O) and 49 of the Fisheries and Aquatic Resources (Amendment) Act 2023, which criminalises Indian fishermen and imposes exorbitant fines;
(b) whether any steps are being taken to seek repealment or amendment of these laws through diplomatic engagement; and
(c) whether more than 3800 Indian fishermen, particularly from coastal districts of Tamil Nadu have been arrested by Sri Lankan authorities since 2014, and if so, the steps taken to bring permanent resolution to this issue?

(a) the details of funds allocated by Government for the promotion and development of Indian languages—particularly Hindi, Sanskrit and Tamil—during the last five years, year-wise and language-wise;
(b) whether the Archaeological Survey of India (ASI) has received the final excavation report on Keeladi submitted by archaeologist Shri Amarnath Ramakrishna in January 2023, and if so, the copy of the said report, the nature of modifications or clarifications sought by ASI and the reasons for the delay in its publication; and
(c) list of archaeological excavations approved by Government over the past five years, budget allocated and present status?

(a) whether the actual cost-sharing pattern between Central Government and States under the Pradhan Mantri Matsya Sampada Yojana (PMMSY) is intended to be in the ratio of 60:40, and whether in reality, States, including Tamil Nadu, are bearing up to 73 per cent of the project cost, and if so, the reasons therefor and the details thereof;
